<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">India gains independence, removing the empire's most vital possession</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/new-zealand"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/New%20Zealand.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>New Zealand</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Parliament adopts the Statute of Westminster, completing legislative independence</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/free-hanseatic-city-of-bremen"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Free%20Hanseatic%20City%20of%20Bremen.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Free Hanseatic City of Bremen</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Land of Bremen is re-established with Bremerhaven</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/british-raj"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/British%20Raj.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>British Raj</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independence and partition create India and Pakistan on 14–15 August</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/myanmar"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Myanmar.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Myanmar</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Aung San and minority leaders agree to form a union at the Panglong Conference</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/hebrew"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hebrew.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hebrew</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The first Dead Sea Scrolls, including the oldest known manuscripts of the Hebrew Bible, are found near Qumran</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/indian-independence-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Indian%20independence%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Indian independence movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British rule ends, and British India is partitioned into India and Pakistan</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/colonial-rule"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Colonial%20rule.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Colonial rule</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British India becomes independent as India and Pakistan, amid the violence of partition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/government/constitutional-monarchy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Constitutional%20monarchy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Constitutional monarchy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Japan’s new constitution makes the emperor “the symbol of the State and of the unity of the people”</span></li></ul></section>
